  "$comment": "Shot list for the Board demo. Paths are relative to the repo root. Each shot uses the first source that exists: a take in the clips folder whose file name starts with `clip`, then each still in order. Takes: `in` skips seconds at the start, `speed` > 1 plays faster, the shot is always `dur` seconds (a short take holds its last frame). Stills: `from`/`to` are [centerX, centerY, zoom] as fractions of the image (after `crop`), eased over the shot; `crop` is [x, y, w, h] fractions, e.g. to drop browser chrome. `v` is the horizontal center (0..1 of the 16:9 frame) of the square window used for the 9:16 cut, or [start, end] to pan; the shot-level `v` applies to takes, the still-level one to that still. `clipCrop` is a default `crop` for every take.",
